 "caveat": "Earnings yield and a Treasury bill rate are not the same kind of return. The bill is a contractual rate paid in cash; an earnings yield is the company's profit measured against its share price, and a shareholder receives only what is paid out as dividend. The comparison shows what the price is asking you to accept, not what you will be paid."
